The tabs of the tabbed and stacked containers of i3, for the shell, see docs/i3.md.

The shell shows the tabs in its bar, see modules/tabs, and i3 draws nothing for them: the colors of the tabs are transparent, with no
title and no icon. What the shell needs of i3 is three things. The room that i3 keeps above a tabbed container is 2 points, not
the height of the font and 4 px, and it does not follow the font. The windows of a split inside tabs get the gap between them,
which i3 gives only to the windows of a split that is not in tabs, and the container of the tabs gives the one at the edges. And
the tabs that are not in front are not mapped when the one in front is a split of windows: i3 keeps them mapped, under the
one in front, and one of them is seen through the gap. If the build stops here, the source of i3 has changed.

